From 4e7178a9f2d971b57ee9a7728ba72203144890ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:16:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: expire kill cooldown across runner sessions

The kill cooldown was stored as an absolute loop number while the loop
counter restarts in every runner process, so a persisted value blocked the
first loops of every later session and consumed each entry signal.
es_daily_trend_v1 was locked out this way from 2026-07-09. Store the cooldown
as remaining blocked loops carried across processes; convert and cap a
leftover legacy value once; clamp any stored value to the longest configured
cooldown. A signal change that arrives during a cooldown is still dropped, as
before. Single-symbol path only.

Review: reproduced by Codex on Python 3.12; human review recorded in the work
log. Not deployed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
