+## 2026-10-02 - Kill cooldown persisted across sessions blocks ES entries
+
+- AUDITOR (Claude, separate thread from the Codex sessions): operator asked why
+  `es_daily_trend_v1` has no fill since 2026-07-09 while the signal reads long.
+- SHOWN (local paper state, read-only copies): `loss_streak=3` and
+  `kill_until=51` for `coinbase:BTC/USDT:sma_200_trend`, both written
+  2026-07-09T00:03:59Z. `paper_sim_monitor.history.jsonl` shows `kill_cooldown`
+  then `signal_action=buy, signal_changed=false, action=None` on each day
+  checked from 2026-07-20 to 2026-10-02. Sessions run 63 loops.
+- Cause: `kill_until` held an absolute loop number while `loops` restarts at 0
+  in each runner process, so loops 1-50 of every session were blocked. The
+  hold->buy change was persisted before the kill gate, so the entry edge was
+  consumed while blocked. `kill_until` only resets after an entry passes the
+  risk check, so the lockout did not expire.
+- ENGINEER: `strategy_runner.py` now stores the cooldown as remaining blocked
+  loops (`kill_remaining:*`), decremented per blocked loop and carried across
+  processes. A leftover legacy `kill_until` is converted once (loops below it
+  were blocked, capped at the longest configured cooldown) and cleared.
+  Loss limits, sizing, exits, entry policy and warm-up are unchanged. An
+  in-process arm still blocks 49 loops, as before.
+- First version also replayed a signal change that arrived while blocked.
+  Independent reviewer subagent returned REJECT: that froze `last_action`
+  across the cooldown and dropped a later legitimate entry (reproduced), and it
+  allowed same-session re-entry after a 3-loss kill. Removed. A change that
+  arrives while blocked is still dropped, as on master. Reviewer also found an
+  off-by-one, an uncapped legacy value and a swallowed state-read error; all
+  corrected, with tests.
+- Re-review of the corrected diff by a second reviewer subagent returned
+  ACCEPT_WITH_RISK: 75 differential scenarios against master within one
+  process showed no difference in orders or final state. It found the
+  risk-block arm site untested; a test was added afterwards and has not itself
+  been re-reviewed. Reviewer subagents are the same model family as the
+  author; human review is still required.
+- After Codex's local review (63 passed on Python 3.12; 13 supplied tests fail
+  on base): a stored `kill_remaining` above the longest configured cooldown is
+  now clamped on read, and the legacy conversion order is pinned by a test (an
+  interrupted conversion repeats the block once; it does not drop it).
+- Scope, per that review: this change is for the single-symbol path only.
+  Monitor history shows every ES kill_cooldown status with
+  `symbols=["BTC/USDT"]`. Two inherited defects are NOT addressed here and need
+  their own reviewed changes: decision and kill logic sit outside the
+  per-symbol loop (only the last symbol is acted on), and the kill gate also
+  blocks protective sells.
+- Rollback note: master ignores `kill_remaining`, so reverting during a
+  cooldown drops the remaining block.
+- Behaviour differences that remain: the cooldown counts loops that reach the
+  kill gate, where master counted every loop; a legacy value blocks 49 loops
+  once, where master blocked 50 in every session. Risk-blocked, scale-blocked
+  and open-intent entries still consume their edge; not addressed here.
+- Why: smallest change that makes the configured cooldown expire. PR #602 does
+  not touch the kill gate and would not lift this lockout.
